VALUES ('4c177be2-d326-5b96-a07c-b527ba531781'::uuid, 'e2e747e7-0aba-5a21-95bf-afd6abda0dd3'::uuid, 'express'::public.lte_6e_stage, 4, 'Explain the Evidence Classification Register: why it is needed, how to complete it, required evidence, quality criteria and prohibited actions.', 'The generated response contains several claims, but the reviewer cannot tell which are supported, conflicting, unsupported, uncertain or missing required evidence. The learner must split the response into claim units and classify each claim against the supplied evidence without deciding the customer outcome.', '{"course_problem": "Northstar Retail is preparing a GenAI customer-support assistant that answers customer questions using approved business information. A generated response appears polished and confident, but the supplied records may show conflict with an approved source, internal-use information appearing in customer-facing output, incomplete review evidence, unclear source or review status, and deadline pressure encouraging premature use. The learner must inspect supplied records, identify workflow objects, classify evidence, recognise visible quality, evidence and boundary signals, record uncertainty, organise a safe review handoff and prepare a permitted first review action without diagnosing the technical cause, changing the response, approving the output or closing the case.", "module_problem": "The generated response contains several claims, but the reviewer cannot tell which are supported, conflicting, unsupported, uncertain or missing required evidence. The learner must split the response into claim units and classify each claim against the supplied evidence without deciding the customer outcome.", "artifact": "Evidence Classification Register", "artifact_statement": "Create a traceable register that lists each controlled claim, the evidence checked, the correct classification, exact supporting excerpt, uncertainty and a neutral reviewer note."}'::jsonb, TRUE)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
